      "text": "To find the number of the first day that ends with the colony having more than 100 bacteria, we need to determine the number of days it takes for the colony to reach this number. \n\nLet's start by writing out the pattern:\n\nDay 0: 3 bacteria\nDay 1: 6 bacteria (twice the previous amount, 3 x 2)\nDay 2: 12 bacteria (twice the previous amount, 6 x 2)\nDay 3: 24 bacteria (twice the previous amount, 12 x 2)\nDay 4: 48 bacteria (twice the previous amount, 24 x 2)\n\nAt this point, we have confirmed that the colony doubles in size every day. We wanted to find the day count when the colony size was over 100:\n\nDay 0: 3 bacteria\nDay 1: 6 bacteria\nDay 2: 12 bacteria\nDay 3: 24 bacteria\nDay 4: 48 bacteria\nDay 5: 96 bacteria\nDay 6: 192 bacteria\n\nSince 192 bacteria is the first number greater than 100, the number of the first day when the colony has more than 100 bacteria is Day 6. Therefore, we put \\boxed{6} for the final answer.\nThe answer is: 6",
